-- title:
--   Generic point of the Weierstrass model factors through the Z-chart
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian integral domain and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$ whose associated projective curve `W.toProjective` is elliptic. Write $X = \mathrm{Proj}$ of the grading on $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 3)\ R$ modulo the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic, the grading being the image of the homogeneous-submodule grading under the quotient map, and let its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ be `Proj.toSpecZero` followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra map from $R$ to the degree-zero part. The statement first records, as instances used to formulate it, that this structure morphism is smooth and geometrically integral and hence that $X$ is an integral scheme, so that its function field is available, and that the function field is an $R$-algebra via the ring map whose $\operatorname{Spec}$ is the canonical map from the stalk at the generic point followed by the structure morphism. The assertion is then that there is an $R$-algebra homomorphism $\psi$ from the homogeneous localisation away from the class of the variable $X_2$ to the function field of $X$ such that the canonical morphism $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the stalk at the generic point into $X$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\psi)$ followed by the $i = 2$ inclusion of the affine open cover of $X$ by the three charts away from the classes of $X_0, X_1, X_2$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that the generic point of an irreducible scheme lies in every nonempty open subscheme, applied to the $Z$-chart of the projective Weierstrass model; it provides the chart-factorisation setup in which the generic point is evaluated in affine coordinates. It is used by [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_genericPoint_chartFactor_pointClass_ne_zero`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_genericPoint_chartFactor_pointClass_ne_zero) and by [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_genericPoint_chartFactor_addMap_self_ne_zeroClass`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_genericPoint_chartFactor_addMap_self_ne_zeroClass).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassProjModel_kw_ev_genericPoint_zChart_factor.lean

